-## Documentation
+`TipJar` is `Ownable` and holds one immutable ERC-20, set at deploy time to Base USDC.
 
-Visit our [docs](https://docs.scaffoldeth.io) to learn how to start building with Scaffold-ETH 2.
+| | |
+| --- | --- |
+| `tip(uint256 amount, string message)` | Pulls `amount` via `transferFrom` and appends to the feed. Needs an allowance first. |
+| `getTips(uint256 offset, uint256 limit)` | One page of the feed, newest first. |
+| `tipCount()` / `totalTipped()` / `jarBalance()` | Feed length, all-time total, current balance. |
+| `withdraw(address to, uint256 amount)` | Owner only. |
 
-To know more about its features, check out our [website](https://scaffoldeth.io).
+Messages are capped at 140 bytes and amounts at `uint96`, which bounds the cost of a `getTips` page.
 
-## Contributing to Scaffold-ETH 2
+**The feed is stored on-chain and read with `eth_call`, not reconstructed from `Tipped` logs.** The
+published site is a static bundle with no indexer behind it, and public RPCs cap how far back
+`eth_getLogs` may reach — a paginated view call keeps working however old the jar gets. The
+`Tipped` event is still emitted for anything that does want to index it.
 
